  "reason": "The source assertion 'Neurons generate action potentials' implies that the event/action (action potentials) is produced by the source (neurons). The relation 'caused_by' defines SOURCE as the explicit event produced by TARGET. Here, if we map the intended fact to the relation structure: Action Potentials (SOURCE of the relation) are caused_by Neurons (TARGET of the relation). This matches the biological causality where neurons produce action potentials. Other relations like 'supplies' or 'carries' imply transport rather than generation/causation. 'describes' lacks direction and causality. Thus, 'caused_by' is the only relation that captures the generative causal link while respecting the fixed endpoints (action potentials as the event, neurons as the cause)."
